1
00:00:00,198 --> 00:00:09,923
(Q11&12（多选）) Presenter: This evening we’re delighted to welcome Dan Beagle, who’s just written a book on looking for and finding food in the wild.

2
00:00:09,923 --> 00:00:16,136
He’s going to tell us everything we need to know about picking wild mushrooms.

3
00:00:16,136 --> 00:00:22,241
Dan: Thank you very much. Well, I need to start by talking about safety. Dan：

4
00:00:22,241 --> 00:00:28,729
You really need to know what you’re doing because some mushrooms are extremely poisonous.

5
00:00:28,729 --> 00:00:40,733
Having said that, once you know what to look for, it’s really worth doing for the amazing variety of mushrooms available – which you can’t get in the shops.

6
00:00:40,733 --> 00:01:02,115
[Q13答案句（C）] But of course, you have to be very careful and that’s why I always say you should never consume mushrooms picked by friends or neighbours – always remember that some poisonous mushrooms look very similar to edible ones and it’s easy for people to get confused.

7
00:01:02,115 --> 00:01:21,687
[Q14答案句（B） - 信号词 - the other thing to avoid is = 对应题干warnings] The other thing to avoid is mushrooms growing beside busy roads for obvious reasons. But nothing beats the taste of freshly picked mushrooms – don’t forget that the ones in the shops are often several days old and past their best.

8
00:01:21,687 --> 00:01:28,626
(Q13&14) There are certain ideas about wild mushrooms that it’s important to be aware of.

9
00:01:28,626 --> 00:01:39,946
Don’t listen to people who tell you that it’s only OK to eat mushrooms that are pale or dull – this is completely untrue.

10
00:01:39,946 --> 00:01:44,786
[Q13答案句（D）] Some edible mushrooms are bright red, for example.

11
00:01:44,786 --> 00:01:56,189
[Q13干扰项（A） ； 排除依据：not necessary to peel] Personally, I prefer mushrooms cooked but it won’t do you any harm to eat them uncooked in salads – it’s not necessary to peel them.

12
00:01:56,189 --> 00:02:11,098
[Q14干扰项（E） ； 排除依据：not necessary to peel] Another thing you should remember is that you can’t tell if a mushroom is safe to eat by its smell – some of the most deadly mushrooms have no smell and taste quite nice, apparently.

13
00:02:11,098 --> 00:02:20,607
[Q14答案句（B）] Finally, just because deer or squirrels eat a particular mushroom doesn’t mean that you can.

14
00:02:20,607 --> 00:02:32,593
(Q15（单选）) Of course, mushroom picking is associated with the countryside but if you haven’t got a car, your local park can be a great place to start.

15
00:02:32,593 --> 00:02:41,483
[Q15干扰项（A）； 没有提到选项中的 要choose] There are usually a range of habitats where mushrooms grow, such as playing fields and wooded areas.

16
00:02:41,483 --> 00:02:51,942
[Q15答案句（C）： first thing in the morning = early； Q15干扰项B wildlife：未提及disturb] But you need to be there first thing in the morning, as there’s likely be a lot of competition – not just from people but wildlife too.

17
00:02:51,942 --> 00:02:57,103
The deer often get the best mushrooms in my local park.

18
00:02:57,103 --> 00:03:08,489
(Q16) [Q16干扰项C： book ：否定- I would't recommend] If you’re a complete beginner, I wouldn’t recommend going alone or relying on photos in a book, even the one I’ve written!

19
00:03:08,489 --> 00:03:18,806
[Q16干扰项A， 考点在题干，否定： but you can’t always rely on] There are some really good phone apps for identifying mushrooms, but you can’t always rely on getting a good signal in the middle of a wood.

20
00:03:18,806 --> 00:03:27,417
[Q16答案句（B）if possible, you should = possible, 后面跟出正确答案， group 原词✅] If possible, you should go with a group led by an expert – you’ll stay safe and learn a lot that way.

21
00:03:27,417 --> 00:03:34,831
(Q17) Conservation is a really important consideration and you must follow a few basic rules.

22
00:03:34,831 --> 00:03:42,973
[Q17答案句（B） can't ... all + only enough for your own needs = a limited amount] You should never pick all the mushrooms in one area – collect only enough for your own needs.

23
00:03:42,973 --> 00:03:49,429
Be very careful that you don’t trample on young mushrooms or other plants.

24
00:03:49,429 --> 00:03:57,366
And make sure you don’t pick any mushrooms that are endangered and protected by law.

25
00:03:57,366 --> 00:04:04,315
(Q18) There’s been a decline in some varieties of wild mushrooms in this part of the country.

26
00:04:04,315 --> 00:04:18,866
[Q18干扰项（A） + 转折(but the biggest problem ) + Q18答案句（C） so many = rise] Restaurants are becoming more interested in locally sourced food like wild mushrooms, but the biggest problem is that so many new houses have been built in this area in the last ten years.

27
00:04:18,866 --> 00:04:28,333
[Q18干扰项B： 只说到了水， 和rain没有关系] And more water is being taken from rivers and reservoirs because of this, and mushroom habitats have been destroyed.

28
00:04:28,333 --> 00:04:33,514
(Q19) Anyway, a word of advice on storing mushrooms.

29
00:04:33,514 --> 00:04:37,622
[Q19干扰项B， 提到brown bag,但和 dark room无关。排除。] Collect them in a brown paper bag and as soon as you get home,&nbsp;

30
00:04:37,622 --> 00:04:45,999
[Q19答案句（A） a couple of days = 2 days , but its' best to cook them asap = no more than] put them in the fridge. They’ll be fine for a couple of days, but it’s best to cook them as soon as possible,

31
00:04:45,999 --> 00:04:49,498
[Q19干扰项（C） ， 只是说需要在wash 之后储存， 但不是题干 「should」这样做。   ‘放得住’不代表‘建议你放着’，更不代表‘洗完以后再放着’。”    - 课堂举例： 一份作业， 从发布到提交限时72小时，在系统中存3天，不会丢，但最好检查完就尽快提交。——你should做的是 让他自己保存， 还是 尽快提交作业？] after washing them really carefully first, of course.

32
00:04:49,498 --> 00:04:54,577
(Q20) So everybody knows what a mushroom tastes like, right?

33
00:04:54,577 --> 00:05:00,575
Well, you’ll be surprised by the huge variety of wild mushrooms there are.

34
00:05:00,575 --> 00:05:08,924
[Q20答案句（A）] Be adventurous! They’re great in so many dishes – stir fries, risottos, pasta.

35
00:05:08,924 --> 00:05:20,626
But just be aware that some people can react badly to certain varieties so it’s a good idea not to eat huge quantities to begin with.

36
00:05:20,626 --> 00:05:23,126
OK, so now I’m going to show you …

